WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.670
- It's still going into
talking about mental health,

00:00:01.670 --> 00:00:02.550
especially right now.

00:00:02.550 --> 00:00:04.830
I think we're all like
everyone on the planet

00:00:04.830 --> 00:00:07.490
is playing some kind of mental game,

00:00:07.490 --> 00:00:08.420
you know, at some point,

00:00:08.420 --> 00:00:10.670
just because it's, you're so isolated,

00:00:10.670 --> 00:00:13.410
your world has completely
changed from your daily routine

00:00:13.410 --> 00:00:15.060
and your kids are, you know,

00:00:15.060 --> 00:00:15.920
if you have kids in your house,

00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:17.290
that's a whole other thing and they,

00:00:17.290 --> 00:00:18.500
and those poor little dudes,

00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:19.940
they're all like, they're,

00:00:19.940 --> 00:00:21.410
they're just running around
going what's happening.

00:00:21.410 --> 00:00:22.243
My mom,

00:00:22.243 --> 00:00:23.076
my little six year old is like,

00:00:23.076 --> 00:00:24.360
is there sickness still happening?

00:00:24.360 --> 00:00:25.193
And I'm like, no.

00:00:25.193 --> 00:00:26.060
- Yeah.

00:00:26.060 --> 00:00:27.880
You know, for a minute,

00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:29.600
when quarantine had first started,

00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:32.750
I was hiding my emotions from my kids

00:00:32.750 --> 00:00:37.390
because I didn't want them
to see mom kind of like

00:00:37.390 --> 00:00:38.223
- Yeah.

00:00:38.223 --> 00:00:39.056
- you know all over the place.

00:00:39.056 --> 00:00:41.250
I always say that I'm kind
of like bipolar, right?

00:00:41.250 --> 00:00:43.260
One minute I'm like, yeah, I got this,

00:00:43.260 --> 00:00:46.010
and then the next minute, I'm
like, no, I don't got this,

00:00:46.010 --> 00:00:47.553
but I found that holding it in--

00:00:47.553 --> 00:00:49.900
- I think that's called
being human and a mom,

00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:50.881
but--

00:00:50.881 --> 00:00:53.510
(laughing)

00:00:53.510 --> 00:00:54.743
- Thank you girl,

00:00:55.820 --> 00:00:56.653
but yeah,

00:00:56.653 --> 00:00:59.230
but I found out that when
I was just holding it in,

00:00:59.230 --> 00:01:01.230
I remember I had meditated
for the first time

00:01:01.230 --> 00:01:03.070
during quarantine, which had been a while.

00:01:03.070 --> 00:01:05.650
I was just like focusing on
everybody else and not myself,

00:01:05.650 --> 00:01:06.526
you know what I mean?

00:01:06.526 --> 00:01:08.150
And moms tend to do that a lot

00:01:08.150 --> 00:01:12.410
and I just started crying.

00:01:12.410 --> 00:01:15.890
Like everything just
started to just, you know,

00:01:15.890 --> 00:01:18.030
let go and release.

00:01:18.030 --> 00:01:18.863
And it was very,

00:01:18.863 --> 00:01:19.870
it was very healthy for me.

00:01:19.870 --> 00:01:22.150
So my point in sharing that story is,

00:01:22.150 --> 00:01:23.340
you know, during this time,

00:01:23.340 --> 00:01:25.510
if anybody, you know, wants some advice,

00:01:25.510 --> 00:01:27.060
especially when it comes
to your mental health,

00:01:27.060 --> 00:01:29.790
number one know that you are worth it.

00:01:29.790 --> 00:01:30.623
You know what I mean?

00:01:30.623 --> 00:01:33.130
Know that you are worth
taking that time out

00:01:33.130 --> 00:01:35.950
to give yourself some sort of self care

00:01:35.950 --> 00:01:38.230
and that's exactly what you know I did.

00:01:38.230 --> 00:01:39.750
And it, and it really helped me.

00:01:39.750 --> 00:01:42.150
And it's helping me during this whole,

00:01:42.150 --> 00:01:45.690
this whole crazy situation
that we're in right now

00:01:45.690 --> 00:01:49.210
is just taking time out,
you know, for yourself.

00:01:49.210 --> 00:01:50.440
- And I think, I think you're right.

00:01:50.440 --> 00:01:51.273
I think moms,

00:01:51.273 --> 00:01:54.550
especially just in my experience
with moms and dads I know,

00:01:54.550 --> 00:01:56.640
it's, it's more than moms that always

00:01:56.640 --> 00:02:00.660
we, we are so worried about
everybody else's stuff

00:02:00.660 --> 00:02:02.780
like their mental health,
how they're doing,

00:02:02.780 --> 00:02:04.050
checking in with them,

00:02:04.050 --> 00:02:04.883
- Yeah.

00:02:04.883 --> 00:02:05.716
- making sure their needs are being met

00:02:05.716 --> 00:02:08.960
and you we are the last
ones that we look at.

00:02:08.960 --> 00:02:10.700
And that is so disruptive,

00:02:10.700 --> 00:02:11.533
not just for you,

00:02:11.533 --> 00:02:13.230
but your family as well.

00:02:13.230 --> 00:02:14.803
- That's a great perspective.

